
Build a PC from Scratch
____________________________________________________

1. Necessary Components
  Processor (CPU): The brain of the machine.
  Motherboard: Connects all components.
  RAM Memory: Necessary to run games and applications.
  Storage: SSD (preferred) or HDD for the system and files.
  Power Supply (PSU): Power for the components.
  Graphics Card (GPU): Essential for gaming and high performance.
  Case: Box to house the parts.
  Cooler: For cooling the processor.

2. Step-by-Step Assembly
  Prepare the Motherboard: Outside the case, place the motherboard on a non-conductive surface.
  Install the Processor: Open the CPU socket on the motherboard, align the processor triangle with the one on the board and gently insert it (without forcing).
  Install the RAM Memory: Open the slot latches and press the modules until you hear a click.
  Install the M.2 SSD (if present): Fit the NVMe SSD into the dedicated slot and screw it in.
  Apply Thermal Paste and Cooler: Apply a small amount to the processor and attach the cooler.
  Install the Motherboard in the Case: Attach the motherboard I/O shield to the case, place the standoffs and screws.
  Install the Power Supply (PSU): Screw the power supply into the case.
  Install the Graphics Card (GPU): Fit it into the motherboard's PCIe slot and screw it into the case.
  Connections: Connect the 24-pin cable (motherboard), 8-pin cable (CPU), the power supply cables to the GPU, and the front panel of the case.

3. Finalization
  Organize the cables to improve airflow.
  Connect the monitor, keyboard, and mouse.
  Plug it into the power outlet, start the PC, install the operating system and drivers.

4. Important Tips
  Use an anti-static wrist strap or touch something grounded in metal to avoid damaging the components.
  Check the motherboard manual to confirm compatibility.
